1
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:33,500
Harry Potter: A History Of Magic is a documentary film directed by Jude Ho.

2
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:01,000
A thrilling journey through legends, belief and folklore, this film goes behind the scenes with the British Library as they search to
tell that story through objects in their collection, in an ambitious new exhibition: Harry Potter: A History Of Magic.

3
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:28,500
Rowling, who is lending unseen manuscripts, drawings and drafts from her private archives (which will sit alongside treasures from the British Library, as well as original drafts and drawings from Jim Kay)
talks about some of the personal items she has lent to the exhibition and gives new insight into her writing, looking at some of the objects from the exhibition that have fired her imagination.

4
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Narrator, played by Imelda Staunton.

5
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:23,500
Herself, played by J.K. Rowling.

6
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Himself, played by David Thewlis.

