10
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:41,000
In the fictional universe of Harry Potter, magic is depicted as a
supernatural force that overrides the laws of nature.

11
00:27:02,500 --> 00:27:08,500
In humans, magical ability is inborn and is usually inherited.

12
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:36,000
Most children of magical parents are magical themselves.

13
00:31:57,500 --> 00:32:03,500
These are called Half-Bloods/Purebloods and are common.

14
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Some children of "Muggle" (non-magical) parents also display magical abilities.

15
00:36:52,500 --> 00:36:58,500
These are called Muggleborns and these are uncommon.

16
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:26,000
Children who are born to wizard parents but cannot perform magic
are called Squibs although these are very rare.

17
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:53,500
Known Squibs in Harry Potter are Mrs Figg and Argus Filch.

18
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:21,000
Rowling, the creator of Harry Potter, based many magical elements in her
fictional universe on real-world mythology and folklore.

19
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:48,500
She has described this derivation as "a way of giving texture to the world".

20
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:16,000
The magic of Harry Potter was the subject of a 2017 British
Library exhibition and an accompanying documentary.

21
00:51:37,500 --> 00:51:43,500
The exhibition, entitled Harry Potter: A History of Magic, was the first at the
British Library to be based on a single series by a living author.

22
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:11,000
The film explores themes of magic, sorcery, wizard,
psychotronic filmmaking, artefacts.

23
00:56:32,500 --> 00:56:38,500
The tone is intense.
